# The game file, the .nup Lichii plays. Without it this machine cannot start a game or read the game's tables. A place
# takes it as an absolute path with no colon.
GAME_TESTING_GAME_FILE=
# kaepora-dump from Kaepora's build, the program that reads the game file's tables for the library.
GAME_TESTING_PATCHER=
# How many games this machine runs at once. One game holds about 13 GB at control.
GAME_TESTING_PLACES=1
# The machine's graphics card, nvidia or amd. An NVIDIA card needs NVIDIA's Container Toolkit.
GAME_TESTING_CARD=nvidia
# The folder of an unpacked Lichii Linux release, the one that holds the lichii program. An absolute path with no colon.
GAME_TESTING_LICHII=
# Where the library keeps its places, in place of ~/.local/share/game-testing. Set this, never XDG_DATA_HOME, which
# also moves podman's store.
GAME_TESTING_DATA=
# The port serve listens on, on 127.0.0.1 only. A tunnel you run gives it reach from other machines.
GAME_TESTING_PORT=7480
# The one token serve takes, and run sends to a far machine. It is as strong as a shell on the game's machine: whoever
# holds it can send a script, and the script runs there as the user who runs serve. Make a long random one, such as
# openssl rand -hex 32 prints. serve does not start without it.
GAME_TESTING_TOKEN=
# A far machine's serve, such as http://127.0.0.1:7481 at this end of an ssh tunnel, with no name or password in it: the
# token goes in GAME_TESTING_TOKEN. With it set, run runs its scripts here against that machine's game, and runs lists
# that machine's records.
GAME_TESTING_URL=
# Traces go to an OTLP collector when both are set, such as http://127.0.0.1:4318 and otlp; without them nothing is
# sent. A run's record keeps its trace id. The same endpoint also takes logs with OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=otlp and metrics
# with OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=
